WEBVTT

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.870
"Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger"
<i>Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger </i>is a TV anime

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:11.870
"Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger"
that was made in Japan 50 years ago.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.160
that was made in Japan 50 years ago.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.830
The story was about a
shape-changing, combining robot

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.000
who traveled through the universe,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.410
but since mankind made
first contact with actual aliens

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.830
soon after it started airing,
its storyline became stale,

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.160
and it was canceled after a single season.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.200
I get that the robot was created
based on the anime,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.660
but what is it doing aboard this spaceship?

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.790
This spaceship was your father's, right?

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.120
Yeah, he said something about
getting it in a trade with some aliens.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.870
Still, I get the feeling that I've
seen this anime before somewhere.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.750
This anime is at least half a century old.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.290
Yeah, I know.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.620
We're about to go to warp.
Get back to the cockpit.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.910
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.700
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.660
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.080
"Hizakuriger was an anime from 50 years ago"
"What's it doing inside the Nagaya Voyager?"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.370
"And now a new peril befalls Robby and Hatchi!"
"Pique on Planet Pluto"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.000
"And now a new peril befalls Robby and Hatchi!"
"Pique on Planet Pluto"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.870
All right,

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.750
we're heading out of the solar system now--

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.330
Wh-What was that?

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.330
--You in the spaceship!
--Huh?

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.500
Warp-out at once!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.540
A debt collector?

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.830
That isn't one of Yang's spaceships.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.660
Did you borrow from someone else?

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.250
No...

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.250
I had all my debts consolidated
with Yang by a crooked lawyer.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.160
Low, easy payments,
and no consultation necessary.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.950
Just honest, clean debt.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.290
What part of any of that
do you have to be proud of?

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.910
Warp-out!

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.620
Huh?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.620
Where are we?

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.620
It looks like Pluto.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.790
Pluto?!

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:28.120
We were trying to fly out
of the solar system, though.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.290
Still, you don't often get a chance
to see Pluto up close like this.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.200
I wouldn't say that.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.080
It isn't even a stage station planet
on the Galaxy Highway,

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.620
and nobody's curious enough
to come all the way here to see it.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.910
Hey, you!

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.250
Follow me! Land your ship!

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.080
Huh? Screw you!

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.790
Ikku, take us to warp again.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.370
I can't. We got tossed all around,
and everything's messed up.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.580
Let's land and let me fix it!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.120
Okay.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.870
It's freezing.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.620
This is supposed to have
been terraformed, too.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.660
It's about the same as being
at the South Pole, isn't it?

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:16.580
Being too cold is making this more fun.
See? My teeth are chattering!

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.450
Welcome to...

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:38.000
W-W-Welcome to Pluto!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.200
Mr. Pluto?!

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.160
Mr. Plato?

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:46.290
No, Mr. Pluto. He's a PR character
from back when people on Earth

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.660
were researching fusion reactors.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.290
How do you know about him?

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.750
I once tried to collect complete
sets of various trading cards,

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:56.200
because I was told it would make me money.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.410
So, did it?

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.910
No comment.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:00.750
Denshi is important!

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:01.910
Ms. Denshi!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:02.790
Ms. Denshi?

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.200
I remember Ms. Denshi.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.120
One day, she just suddenly disappeared, huh?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.250
What are the two of you doing on Pluto?

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.660
It's because we...

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:19.620
--...are now PR characters for Pluto!
--...are now PR characters for Pluto!

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.410
I didn't know that.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.370
Pluto, planet of dreams and romance!

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:28.000
Have a lovely vacation on the
farthest planet from the sun!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.580
But it's not a planet.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.750
It's not a planet;
it's become a planetoid, right?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:34.910
Yeah, right.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.660
--We're not a 'toid!
--We're not a 'toid!

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.790
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:42.660
Besides, we didn't <i>become </i>a planetoid!
We were <i>made </i>a planetoid!

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.830
Dummy! Dummy! Dummy!

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.000
We are the victims of the solar system!

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.080
Denshi is important!

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.080
No, no, wait, wait!
I don't get what's going on!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.750
You inside there... You inside there,
please come out and talk to us.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.830
All right, let us start from the top.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.580
This way, please.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.620
I am the Pluto Travel Bureau chief.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.120
I am his daughter.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.120
Not this whole pattern again.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:20.910
Is this becoming a thing now?

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:26.910
As you may know, our Pluto was
demoted from planet to planetoid.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.290
Unilaterally, without anyone
asking for our input.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.120
Well, Pluto is smaller in size
than Earth's moon,

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.330
--so it's too small to be called a planet--

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.790
--I object to us being compared to a moon!
If anything, that's the problem!
--so it's too small to be called a planet--

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.370
--I object to us being compared to a moon!
If anything, that's the problem!

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:48.000
We get called a planetoid, whereas the moon,
a satellite--a common satellite...

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.410
A common satellite gets to have Monday,
its own day of the week!

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.870
Tuesday through Saturday are fine,
since those are all planets.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:59.410
But Monday is named for a moon!
A <i>moon</i>! A satellite!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.700
You get it, don't you?

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.580
--Uh, yeah.
--Uh, yeah.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.660
We Plutonians demand that
Pluto be restored as a planet!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.410
That's crazy.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.870
Also, we seek that Monday
be changed to be Plutoday.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.750
The moon won't agree to that.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:20.500
--Make Mondays Plutodays!
--Make Mondays Plutodays!

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.500
--♪ Make Mondays Plutodays,
<i>tyurya tyurya tyurya </i>♪

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.580
--The chanting of the Plutonian citizens
is surging down Main Street.
--♪ Make Mondays Plutodays,
<i>tyurya tyurya tyurya </i>♪

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.790
♪ <i>tyurya tyurya tyuryarya</i>! ♪

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.830
♪ Leave Tuesday as Tuesday,
<i>tyurya tyurya tyurya</i>! ♪

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:35.040
Wow, they're getting their
<i>tyurya</i>-<i>tyurya </i>on! Yay! Yay!

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.040
But they've never even heard of
your movement on Earth or Mars.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.370
That's right! That's exactly right!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:46.080
Where the hell did those two go?

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:50.540
In order for us to plead our case
for restoring us from planetoid to planet,

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:54.790
we hired a major advertising
agency to consult with us.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:59.290
The ad agency said these characters
would be perfect for Pluto.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:03.750
Since they suggested Mr. Pluto,
we adopted them, just like they said.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.200
They came dirt cheap, too.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.450
I'm not sure if that's recycling, or just
a delicate means of inventory disposal.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.620
<i>That </i>one.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.620
They said if we acted now, they'd
throw in Denshi at no extra charge.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.160
And a package deal, at that.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.830
The ad agency said that our own
local specialty was needed

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.450
and told us to sell a signature
product in the form of shave ice,

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.040
using genuine Plutonian ice,

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.040
so we made some.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.040
Shave ice, on this freezing-ass world?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.080
Does it sell?

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.120
--No, it doesn't.
--No doubt.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.580
Hmm, what flavor is this?

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.450
Ah, it's nitrogen!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.330
There's too much nitrogen,
and it isn't very good.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.870
What kind of sommelier are you?!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:44.250
We've kept with the PR activities,
like the ad agency said to,

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.290
but we've seen absolutely no results.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.200
Well, of course not.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.580
--You have your planetoid being
led around by an ad agency.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.700
--We're not a 'toid!
--You have your planetoid being
led around by an ad agency.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.450
Mr. Pluto is getting no traction anywhere else.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.790
His trading card isn't even rare.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:08:59.910
I knew it.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:00.910
Papa...

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:01.870
So,

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:05.410
did you capture us because
you wanted to make that clear?

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.450
You were successful with Mars.

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.410
Just be yourself.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.540
Just be myself.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.330
Ah, that's from when we were on Mars.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:19.040
After watching this broadcast, it all clicked.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:23.160
"Make Pluto a planet!"
"Make Mondays Plutodays!"

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:26.580
We want you two to
take over our PR campaign.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.830
Hold on, hold on!

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.580
We aren't PR men, and we aren't
town revitalization event planners.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:36.910
In fact, he has such bad luck, he's on
his way to Isekandar to drive it out.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:40.040
Then why did you agree
to be on that Martian TV show?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.290
It just happened!

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.250
Please!

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:46.500
Please do it for us!

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:47.330
All right.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:48.580
Hey, Robby!

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:53.450
I'm not some pushover who is easily
moved by a woman's tears or cleavage.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.290
Glance.

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:55.830
Please!

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:59.120
But I can't stand it when
people are taken advantage of!

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.660
You're someone who gets nothing
<i>but </i>taken advantage of, after all.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.910
Let's show that ad agency up!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.830
Oh! All right.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.870
--Thank you very much!
--Thank you very much!

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:15.660
The best thing to do is advance who you
really are, just we did like on Mars.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:18.700
So flat-out, what are Pluto's
actual selling points?

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:19.620
We have none.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.200
Dreams! And romance!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:25.790
Pluto is a planet whose selling points
are dreams and romance!

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:26.620
How so?

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:29.160
From what the ad agency says,

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.790
Pluto has the image of being the most
remote world in the solar system

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:36.200
where battleships and galactic railway
trains stop over, so going forward,

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.750
we should attract visitors with
a Matsu[beep] Memorial Hall.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.080
Whatever became of that idea?

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.200
All they ever tell us is they're
almost ready, just a little longer.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.790
Forget what the ad agency is telling you!

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.870
The key to a tourist attraction
is whether or not female tourists visit.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.830
The 20-to-34-year-old female demographic.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:59.870
That whatever-you-call-it museum
won't draw too many of them.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.410
That's true.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:05.540
Are there any, say, cute creatures
indigenous to Pluto?

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:06.540
Nice thinking.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:09.540
Like Plutonian pandas,
or Plutonian lesser pandas?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.080
Are we limited to pandas?

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:15.540
As long as it's an animal cute enough
to capture a girl's heart, it'll do.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:18.950
Ah, we do have penguins! Plutonian penguins!

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:21.120
See? There's one right there!

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.700
Wow!

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.040
Amazing! Amazing!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.580
Those aren't gonna capture anyone's hearts.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.160
--And speaking of hearts...
--Huh?

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:42.080
We saw a heart-shaped pattern on the
surface of Pluto from space, remember?

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:46.160
Ah, you mean the Tombaugh Regio?

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.750
Oh, you're right, it looks like a heart!

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.540
That will capture girls' hearts.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.660
You can say it's a matchmaking
or love-promoting power spot

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:58.160
and make that a selling point.
"Pluto, the planet of love."

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.040
It's just an icefield that happens
to be shaped like that.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:05.250
Depending on the angle you see it from,
it might be hard to call it a heart.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.120
It doesn't have any love powers.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.330
How come <i>that's </i>the only thing
you're taking seriously?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.870
The fact is, there's a
heart-shaped icefield there!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.450
Erect a shrine to love
and romance or whatever,

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.540
and start selling cute items out of it!

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.120
Like the "Pluto Shrine"?

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.500
How about Ms. Denshi charms?

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.080
Forget about them already!

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:26.870
We've spent a good deal of our
budget on Mr. Pluto already.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:27.790
That we have.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:30.450
Forget about them!

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:31.500
--Okay.
--Okay.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:37.290
If your relationship has grown cold...

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:41.250
If you can't close the distance between you...

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.750
--Leave it to Pluto!
--Leave it to Pluto!

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.080
Wait up! Wait up!

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.250
Go ahead and try to catch me!

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:53.910
Pluto's Heartful Icefield is your
power spot to happiness.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:57.500
Love and affection--it's all right here!

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.200
"Monday"
Make Mondays...

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:00.910
"Plutoday!"
...Plutodays!

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.370
"Plutoday!"
We don't need that last bit.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.000
Just cut out Mr. Pluto's line and it's finished.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.370
Huh? But we already have the characters.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.910
Forget them!

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.910
Sending the finished commercial
to the galactic networks

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.000
and uploading it on U-Chube.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.450
Aww...

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.500
We're just about repaired,
but we still can't go to warp.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.750
There's something we need to do.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.040
So we're on the move.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.080
Off to the heart-shaped icefield.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.450
Stop working your robot so hard!

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.660
Mr. Yang, we've reached Mars!

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.660
Robby and Hatchi must be somewhere on Mars.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.330
Just you wait, Robby.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.330
What is this?

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:48.200
There's nothing here. It's just a desert!

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:50.120
Nobody is selling <i>takoyaki</i>.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:52.580
There's no Takotubo Land.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:55.620
Welcome!

00:13:55.620 --> 00:14:01.620
Welcome to Mars! Would you like to take
the Mars Adventure Experience Tour?

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:05.950
It's a tour with an extreme
temperature differential of -140° to 60°.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:10.040
Enjoy powerful sandstorms
on the Dust Devil Tour.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.700
Or take the Olympus Mons
mountaineering tour,

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.660
which goes to an elevation of 25,000 meters.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.410
We offer many classic Martian tours.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.290
Hey! What happened to the octopuses?!

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.790
--We stopped doing that.
--How come?! How come you stopped?!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.120
When you think Mars, you think octopuses!

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:28.540
Aww, octopuses... I was hoping
like the devilfish to see some...

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:32.580
Mars tourism has changed
its concept extensively.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.290
What about the Martian cabaret clubs?

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.660
We have regular cabaret clubs.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:39.910
Why? How could you?

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:43.910
Why did you change your
policies so suddenly?

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:46.660
We received some advice
from certain individuals.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.000
Was one of them...

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:50.660
...this man?

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.540
Ah, so you know Robby?

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:54.950
Where is he?!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.160
They left Mars a good while ago.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.950
They said something about
heading to Isekandar.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:03.910
Isekandar?! That's in the Andromeda Galaxy!

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:07.580
Let's go! Their destination is Isekandar!

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.540
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:11.580
Isekandar is far away!

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.410
Why would we go there
over someone like Robby?

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:18.000
Shut up! Look, we're going to catch him
before he reaches Isekandar.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.700
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:24.620
Yes! All right, the Cupid Temple
will go over there.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.910
And over here, we'll build the Ragaraja Shrine!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:30.080
And we'll have a big-ass souvenir-shop-lined
street! I'm talking huge! Huge!

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.000
Come up with some new PR characters
that will fit in with this, too.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.250
Okay.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:37.540
That leaves the heart-shaped local
specialties. The question is, what?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.910
Let's make it something warm,
instead of shave ice.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.000
Like <i>oden</i>, or heart-shaped <i>tama konnyaku</i>?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.700
Where's the feminine touch?

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.330
That sort of stuff goes over pretty well.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:53.040
So here's where you went, Chief.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.000
Who's that?

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.330
The people from the major advertising agency.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:16:00.500
"Dontsu Inc."
Dontsu... Incorporated?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.120
I'm Kodai, which is spelled the same way
as in Kodai deceptive advertising.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.660
"Acting Manager Kodai"
I'm Kodai, which is spelled the same way
as in Kodai deceptive advertising.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:04.580
"Acting Manager Kodai"
And I'm the too-good-to-be-true Morisugi.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.290
"Acting Manager Kodai"
"Morisugi"
And I'm the too-good-to-be-true Morisugi.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:10.040
Chief, it's time to celebrate!
It's finally completed!

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:11.200
What is?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.410
The full-size Mr. Pluto!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.450
Huh?

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.370
Incredible, right?

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:28.750
Mr. Pluto is supposed to be 20 meters tall,

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:31.250
and here is a full-size robot!

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.160
I never ordered this.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:36.700
It's part of the new Pluto PR plan.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:39.620
I thought that was the
Matsu[beep] Memorial Hall.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.910
Not to worry. We built it on the cheap.

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:44.950
That's not really helping...

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:49.870
Okay, let's let Mr. Pluto Robo
massively publicize Pluto!

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:53.000
Act now, and we'll also
include a set of spare parts!

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:57.160
Mr. Pluto is from a long bygone era.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.450
So is Ms. Denshi.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.910
Who are these people?

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:05.160
Oh, these are two new people
I've asked to help with Pluto's PR.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:10.000
Chief... what's the point
of asking these amateurs?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.910
Look here at this Mr. Pluto card.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:18.290
Mr. Pluto is a normal card. It was said that,
in time, it would become valuable,

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:21.500
but even after 20 years,
there is absolutely no demand for it!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:27.500
If palming him off is the work of a pro,
then I'm glad to be an amateur!

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.410
Chief...

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:29.330
Hmm?

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:34.040
I thought you contracted our firm
to comprehensively do Pluto's PR.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:38.040
We haven't signed a contract yet
for any supplemental PR.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.330
--Is that true?
--Yes, it is.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.120
Then we have to market that robot,
no matter what it takes!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.250
What do we do?

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.410
It's time for us to flex our muscles!

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:59.870
Chief! At least check out the
performance of the Mr. Pluto Robo!

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.290
Launch!

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.370
--What was that?!
--Hey, watch it!

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:15.250
Never underestimate
an agency's planning ability!

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.910
Why don't you amateurs
clear out of here now?

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:20.370
Yeah! Yeah!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:24.870
Nice giant robot!
Not bad at all! Let's go, Hatchi!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.200
You got it, Robby!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:36.160
Hizakuriger!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:40.540
Kodai, they're sending out a robot, too!

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.160
What kind of amateurs are they?

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:46.620
Okay, so now that we've broken
out Hizakuriger, what do we do?

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:50.120
We're not even entirely
sure this thing can fight.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.250
You were raring to go, too, you know.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.200
I'm not opposed to it.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.830
We're in an unarmed
PR robot. What do we do?

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:01.330
There's nothing to it. We do what
the operations manual says to do.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:04.870
You there, the robot type that
combines together for no reason!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:10.410
Unless you want a taste of my
Plutonium Buster, you'll leave at once!

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:12.500
Plutonium Buster?

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.370
That sounds like a finishing move.

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:16.290
It definitely doesn't sound safe, does it?

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.790
Two can play that game.

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:23.040
No, unless <i>you </i>want a taste of my
Shining Hizakuri Attack, <i>you'll </i>leave!

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.120
What is that?

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:26.950
The ultimate finishing move
that I just thought up!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.080
They're ready to fight.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.580
Damn it.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:33.660
I'll just deflect it with my Pluto Shield!

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:37.870
Well I have the Hizakuri Barrier!
If you want a fight, then let's fight!

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.290
Pluto Saber!

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.370
Hiazkuri Ultimate Buster!

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.200
--Pluto Dynamic Slash!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.330
--What's going to happen, Papa?
--Pluto Dynamic Slash!

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:43.910
--What's going to happen, Papa?
--Hizakuri Galactic Cross Cutter!

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:46.250
--I have absolutely no idea.
--Hizakuri Galactic Cross Cutter!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:49.160
Why? Why isn't he attacking?

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.290
If you're gonna bring it, then bring it.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.830
If he brings it, we're screwed, though.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.000
You don't think...

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.830
Could it be...?

00:19:56.830 --> 00:20:01.250
--He's... weak...?
--He's... weak...?

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.250
Kodai, look at this.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:08.000
Looking at this x-ray image, that robot
is hollow. There's nothing inside!

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.120
Hollow?

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.830
I get it! They transform
and combine for no reason,

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.700
so the space where their hands
and feet come out of is hollow!

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:17.870
But why would they make
a deliberately hollow robot?

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:21.250
Whoever made it must have really liked
transforming and combining robots.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.660
Even though it would be hollow?

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:25.950
The kind of people who like these things
generally have hollow heads, too.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:29.540
Well, we're bluffing, too, but our
robot actually has stuff inside it!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.830
We most likely have this in the bag!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.250
--Here he comes!
--Find us some kind of weapon!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:36.660
Some kind?

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.450
I've got something!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.660
Hizakuri Javelin!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.950
That looked cool!

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.370
That at least looked cool!

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:51.450
Way to bluff! Pluto Punch!

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:52.250
Dodge him! Dodge him!

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.700
I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:55.580
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:56.950
--Eh?
--Eh?

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.620
Huh? H-Huh...?

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:02.500
--Hey...
--Yeah.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:04.750
--Javelin Galactic Thrust!
--Javelin Galactic Thrust!

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:05.870
--Wha--?!
--Wha--?!

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:08.580
We never even completed delivery!

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.040
We won!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.450
That guy was way too weak.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.750
Hey! I've finished repairs.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.450
Okay, let's go!

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.290
Ah! Wait!

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.580
I don't think you'll get
Mondays changed to Plutodays,

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:34.200
but I do think your tourism
will go well, so hang in there!

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.620
See you later!

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.290
Wait!

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:41.000
We still haven't paid their consulting fee.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.200
Eh, what does it matter?

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:50.500
Heh, I really am a heartless fiend.

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:55.120
Repairs are done, so what do you say
we blast on out of this solar system?

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.830
Oh, yeah! Here we come, universe!
Let's head for the future!

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:01.080
Yeah, you don't need to get so excited.

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:11.410
What? They left Earth's system?

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:15.200
Judging by the Smartbracelet credit history,
they're probably already gone.

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.870
This is bad. Call the Luna Guard immediately.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:20.290
Yes, sir!

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:53.120
"Next time"
"#04 Merfolk On the End of the Pole"

00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:57.000
"Next time"
"#04 Merfolk On the End of the Pole"
Next time, "Merfolk On the End of the Pole."

00:23:57.250 --> 00:24:01.950
"After stopping off on the planet Odwarla,"
"Robby is hospitalized with an acute illness"

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.000
"He has an unexpected reunion there?"
"And what about Mr. Yang?"
